# Read Project Documentation

When working on CherryPlay, use the project's **Markdown documentation** as the source of truth for architecture, contracts, setup, and features. Documentation is **cross-linked**: many files reference others; follow those links to get full context.

## Documentation map

**Start here to see what documentation exists:** [DOCUMENTATION_MAP.yaml](DOCUMENTATION_MAP.yaml) in the repository root — a categorized map of all `.md` files (project docs vs Cursor IDE config, entry points, hubs per subsystem).

## When to Read Docs

- **Architecture, API, or contracts** — start from [CONTRACTS.md](CONTRACTS.md), [CherryPlayServer/README.md](CherryPlayServer/README.md), [docs/integration/README.md](docs/integration/README.md).
- **Database and persistence** — [CherryPlayServer/DATABASE.md](CherryPlayServer/DATABASE.md).
- **Operations and deployment** — [CherryPlayServer/OPS.md](CherryPlayServer/OPS.md).
- **Dev setup and quick start** — [DEV_SETUP.md](DEV_SETUP.md), [QUICK_START.md](QUICK_START.md), [README.md](README.md).
- **Terms and identifiers** — [GLOSSARY.md](GLOSSARY.md).
- **Adding a PartyTheme** — [ADDING_THEME.md](ADDING_THEME.md).
- **CherryPlayList (desktop app)** — [CherryPlayList/FULL_DOCUMENTATION.md](CherryPlayList/FULL_DOCUMENTATION.md), [CherryPlayList/TECHNICAL.md](CherryPlayList/TECHNICAL.md), [CherryPlayList/BUILD.md](CherryPlayList/BUILD.md), [CherryPlayList/docs/README.md](CherryPlayList/docs/README.md) and linked modules under `CherryPlayList/docs/modules/`.

## Following Links

- If a doc you read links to another (e.g. `[CONTRACTS.md](../CONTRACTS.md)`, `[DATABASE.md](DATABASE.md)`), **open and read** the linked file when it is relevant to the task.
- Resolve paths relative to the current doc: `../` = parent directory, `./` = same directory.
- Hub docs (README.md, `docs/integration/README.md`, `CherryPlayList/docs/modules/README.md`) list key documents; use them to discover and follow the chain of references.

## Summary

1. Open **[DOCUMENTATION_MAP.yaml](DOCUMENTATION_MAP.yaml)** first to see the full catalog of docs and entry points.
2. Prefer project `.md` docs over guessing when answering questions about setup, API, or behavior.
3. Treat linked docs as part of the same documentation graph; follow links to get complete information.
4. Use the paths above as entry points; from there, follow in-doc links as needed.
5. If docs and code appear inconsistent, report the mismatch explicitly and avoid inventing behavior.
